\"],\n      \"nets\": [\"Net-(U1-EN{slash}CHIP_PU)\", \"GND\"],\n      \"observed\": \"C7 is a 10uF capacitor on the ESP32 EN/CHIP_PU net, with R5 (10k) as the pull-up to +3V3.\",\n      \"expected\": \"The usual ESP32 EN reset RC uses about 0.1\u20131uF with a 10k pull-up. A 10uF value gives a roughly 100 ms time constant and slows reset and power-on sequencing.\",\n      \"evidence\": [\n        {\"source\": \"netlist\", \"quote\": \"(comp (ref \\\"C7\\\") (value \\\"10uF\\\") ... (property (name \\\"LCSC`\\\") (value \\\"C15850\\\"))\"},\n        {\"source\": \"netlist\", \"quote\": \"(net (code \\\"26\\\") (name \\\"Net-(U1-EN{slash}CHIP_PU)\\\") (class \\\"Default\\\") (node (ref \\\"C7\\\") (pin \\\"1\\\") (pintype \\\"passive\\\")) (node (ref \\\"R5\\\") (pin \\\"1\\\") (pintype \\\"passive\\\")) (node (ref \\\"U1\\\") (pin \\\"8\\\")\"}\n      ],\n      \"impact\": \"The slow EN rise may delay boot or cause reset timing problems. The effect is likely minor, and the value may be intentional.\",\n      \"confidence\": 0.25\n    }\n  ],\n  \"summary\": \"The netlist is largely consistent with the specification, but J5 is an undocumented screw terminal wired directly onto the GPIO1 heater-control net beside GND, which is the most likely deviation. The 10uF EN capacitor C7 is a weaker, value-based concern.\"\n}",
